From c234093ee332399353c2891b22ce1ef5d30c3081 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:45:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] test(motion): pin the rest Adaptive raster entry proof
 and the D/80 load ceiling

The raster half of the entry proof had no test of its own: a unit test
now hands Entries a raster holding material the polygon bound does not,
and a plunge onto it is refused (red when the raster half is dropped or
its footprint is 0). The load is pinned on the default D/80 measuring
grid under a documented ceiling of optimal x 1.2, and on a D/240 grid
the corners read within the planner's own margin.

Fixes #2113

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
---
